<title>USA: Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are ticket sales for the top movies at the U.S. box office over the Friday to Sunday weekend, according to estimates by Exhibitor Relations Co. Final data will be released on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (1) Liar Liar ........................ $24.2 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) The Devil's Own .................. $14.3 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) Selena ...........................  $5.6 million</p>
<p>    4 (3) Return of the Jedi ...............  $4.5 million</p>
<p>    5 (*) The Sixth Man ....................  $4.3 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) Jungle 2 Jungle ..................  $4.1 million</p>
<p>    7 (*) Turbo: A Power Rangers Movie .....  $3.5 million</p>
<p>    8(10) The English Patient ..............  $3.0 million</p>
<p>    9 (*) B.A.P.S. .........................  $2.8 million</p>
<p>    10(5) Private Parts ....................  $2.5 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in parentheses are last week's rank.</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;The Devil's Own&quot; is released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Selena&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.. &quot;B.A.P.S.&quot; is released by Time Warner's New Line Cinema.</p>
<p>&quot;Return of the Jedi&quot; and &quot;Turbo: A Power Rangers Movie&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Jungle 2 Jungle&quot; and &quot;The Sixth Man&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co., while &quot;The English Patient&quot; is released by Disney's Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Private Parts&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
